// EXPECT: E0288 — `#must` on a procedure that returns nothing (ADR-0151 §3)
//
// There is no result to receive, so the marker can never be violated and never does anything. Accepted
// silently, it would leave a reader believing a check is running — which is ADR-0058 §3's rule about
// silently-ignored directives, applied to the newest one.
//
// Reported at the **declaration**, which is the mistake's own site, and the call-site check
// deliberately stays quiet for a `void` callee so that one error is not also reported at every call.
log_it :: (n: s64) #must {
    ignored := n;
}

main :: () {
    log_it(0);
}
